# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command cores
shell rust
usage 1   cores ls [--installed|--available|--updates|--unsupported] [<console>]
usage 2                                 one line per libretro core: state, console, id, source, version, size, licence
usage 3   cores info <core>             what is known of one core, as key: value lines
usage 4   cores fetch                   libretro's catalogue and this platform's index fetched again (a network request)
usage 5   cores get <core>...           download, check and install; prints the SHA-256 to approve
usage 6   cores update [<core>...]      the installed cores the index offers a new build of, or those named
usage 7   cores rollback <core>         the build kept by the last update put back in place
usage 8   cores rm <core>...            a downloaded core removed, with its kept build; saves and settings stay
usage 9   cores verify [<core>...]      each installed core checked against its NOTICE, the project's copies refreshed
usage 10   cores approve <core>          trust a downloaded core, by its SHA-256; typed at the prompt only
usage 11   cores default <console> [<engine>]
usage 12                                 the console's engine, printed or set
usage 13   cores default --game <path> [<engine>|-]
usage 14                                 a game's own engine, printed, set or cleared
usage 15   cores wait [cores<n>]         follow a cores job that went on in the background (ps lists them, kill stops one)

case the usage, and what a command line refuses
target none
covers 1-15
$ cores
out 435
Usage: cores ls [--installed|--available|--updates|--unsupported] [<console>] | cores info <core> | cores fetch | cores get <core>... | cores update [<core>...] | cores rollback <core> | cores rm <core>... | cores verify [<core>...] | cores approve <core> | cores default <console> [<engine>] | cores default --game <path> [<engine>|-] | cores wait [cores<n>]
  A core is named by its file's stem, as cores ls prints it. See man cores.
status 1
action none
$ cores get pcsx2
out 189
cores: pcsx2: pcsx2 is not one of the libretro cores EmuSen hosts (pcee2, flycast, snes9x, nestopia, genesis_plus_gx, picodrive, mupen64plus_next, sameboy, mednafen_psx_hw, mednafen_saturn)
status 1
action none
